# CODEOWNERS — Automatic Reviewer Assignment
#
# This file tells GitHub to automatically request a review from the listed
# people whenever a pull request changes the specified files.
#
# This is how you enforce governance: critical scripts cannot be merged
# without sign-off from a senior analyst. Quality and continuity, not policing!
#
# Format: <file pattern>  <@github-username or @org/team>
#
# ── Instructions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Replace @YOUR-GITHUB-USERNAME with your actual GitHub username.
# For team accounts, use @your-org/your-team-name.
# Commit this file to .github/CODEOWNERS for it to take effect.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Default owner for everything in the repository
* @YOUR-GITHUB-USERNAME

# The workshop notebook and any data scripts require senior review
# (these are the files most likely to contain sensitive queries or data)
/workshop/ @YOUR-GITHUB-USERNAME

# The live dashboard — requires sign-off before it goes public
/docs/ @YOUR-GITHUB-USERNAME

# CI/CD and configuration — only trusted admins should change these
/.github/ @YOUR-GITHUB-USERNAME
/.pre-commit-config.yaml @YOUR-GITHUB-USERNAME
